INT. PARKED VAN OUTSIDE BELL FOUNDRY - NIGHT

ZELDA
You're humming.

MURALI
I'm not.

ZELDA
You are. It's the thing from the radio.

MURALI
It's a lullaby.

ZELDA
Whose?

MURALI
Mine. My mother's. Don't.

ZELDA
I didn't say anything.

MURALI
You were about to.

ZELDA
I was about to say it's nice.

MURALI
It isn't nice. It's a song about a goat.

ZELDA
Is it a good goat?

MURALI
He dies.

ZELDA
Ah.

MURALI
Everybody dies in the second verse.

ZELDA
That's a heavy lullaby.

MURALI
We were a heavy family.

ZELDA
And you cope by humming in a van outside a bell foundry.

MURALI
Four more minutes.

ZELDA
Four more minutes.

MURALI
Then we go in.

ZELDA
Then we go in.

MURALI
And you stop asking questions.

ZELDA
Never.
